<title>FRANCE: Air Liberte founder welcomes BA /Rivaud bid.</title>
<headline>Air Liberte founder welcomes BA /Rivaud bid.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lotfi Belhassine, the founder of regional airline Air Liberte, on Wednesday welcomed a takeover bid by British Airways Plc and Vincent Bollore, chairman of banking group Rivaud.</p>
<p>&quot;It's an excellent solution. We keep all the assets. I do not see another French solution, the last deadline was Friday,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
<p>Air Liberte went into administration on September 26. BA's TAT and Vincent Bollore, head of Rivaud, Financiere Moncey and trading group Bollore, made a joint offer to the commercial court today.</p>
</text>
